<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	Prod-only (#0270): this plist ships only in the Prod build — see the
	"Embed Broker" Run Script build phase, which skips embedding entirely
	when PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER is not co.sstools.Batty. That sidesteps
	shipping a Beta build (co.sstools.Batty.beta) with a LaunchAgent whose
	Label collides with Prod's, which #0265's own trap list warns can
	confuse launchd across multiple copies of the app on disk.

	Four strings must stay byte-identical (the "four-string rule" in
	docs/xpc/xpc-cli-architecture.md): this filename (minus .plist), the
	Label below, the MachServices key below, and
	BattyXPCCore/ServiceNames.broker. None of them can be derived from the
	others here — a plist copied into the bundle by a build phase does not
	get $(VAR) build-setting substitution the way Info.plist does. Mismatch
	any one and launchd silently declines to reserve the name.
	-->
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>co.sstools.Batty.broker</string>

	<key>BundleProgram</key>
	<string>Contents/Resources/bin/BattyBroker</string>

	<key>MachServices</key>
	<dict>
		<key>co.sstools.Batty.broker</key>
		<true/>
	</dict>
</dict>
</plist>
